  "slug": "inventory-adjustment-incident-report-form",
  "title": "Inventory Adjustment Incident Report Form",
  "subtitle": "A practical fact-based incident report for inventory adjustment that connects identity, observations and evidence, decision authority, exception ownership, and accountable closeout.",
  "description": "An original retail-operations fact-based incident report for inventory adjustment covering inventory count and adjustment, evidence references, authorization, escalation, operating limits, disposition, and handoff without copying a third-party form.",
  "use_case": "Use when a inventory control lead opens one inventory adjustment record to capture objective facts, protect people and records, document response and notifications, assign follow-up, and close without unsupported conclusions; closure requires a documented outcome, evidence route, responsible owner, and recipient acknowledgment.",
  "risk_tier": "A",
